{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh","id":182714,"title":"Hunger for flesh","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-28T01:36:46-07:00","id":182714,"title":"Hunger for flesh","content":"So one of fundamental part of (pop)cultural werewolf myth is hunger for flesh of humans and animals, just like vampires are hungry for blood of living. In <b>Requiem</b> we got that Kindred can drink blood of beings for Vitea and it's they basic mode of replenishing they &quot;fuel stat&quot;. How this topic looks in the <b>Forsaken</b>?<br /> <br /> Do werewolves are craving for humans meat? I'm remembering something that they got the Essence from eating wolves or man - but how much?<br /> <br /> Would other animals also nourish them, like deers or sheep? There is popular image that young werewolves wake ups on the half eaten body of some deer.<br /> <br /> Are Uratha in Gauru craving more of peoples flesh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T03:43:14-07:00","id":182773,"title":"","content":"Uratha gain Essence from eating human or wolf flesh (p77 WtF) but it is a sin against Harmony (p181 WtF).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T03:44:28-07:00","id":182776,"title":"","content":"Other animals would provide meat to sustain the body, but not Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T03:52:17-07:00","id":182780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=182776#post182776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other animals would provide meat to sustain the body, but not Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the other animals were generating small parts of Essence, how much it would be? I think probably one Essence point for whole deer, or maybe up to Stamina of animal. This way humans and wolves are still far superior prey (and even easier to hunt), but we have image of werewolves eating other animals on day-to-day scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-28-2014, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T07:33:16-07:00","id":182861,"title":"","content":"I think if you wanted werewolves to gain Essence in this way, it shouldn't actually come from eating the animal, but from hunting it. You can't go out and buy some venison to refuel your essence, but if you go into the woods and track down a dear, Harry it, corner it, and kill it with your own claws before eating it, that might be worth a bit of Essence. Though keep in mind, the smell of freshly killed meat can be a Kuruth trigger if your Harmony is too high or too low, as of the Idigam Chronicles, so this would be a risky endeavor if you're not fairly balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:02:42-07:00","id":182996,"title":"","content":"Yeah in the movies and tv shows and books werewolves don't normally eat the things they kill, or if they do, only small portions of it (enough to get blood around their mouth). They're mainly focused on killing, or being the romantic interest of the protagonist.<br /> <br /> Anyways it points out in the core book you get essence for eating certain kinds of flesh, and there's some harmony sins as well, depending on the whys and hows. Other books expand upon it, with lodges being dedicated to eating people, or other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-28-2014, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:20:03-07:00","id":183019,"title":"","content":"Make a variation of the Sacred Hunt aiming animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T18:10:32-07:00","id":183400,"title":"","content":"Hunters in darkness milestone lets them gain essence from anything. Arguably under the new system you can eat people without the super negative harmony of the old. It should be a breaking point from human though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T18:21:02-07:00","id":183406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=183400#post183400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters in darkness milestone lets them gain essence from anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess they don't get essence from mimicking the scene by which American Pie got it's name, but y'know the gist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T00:02:22-07:00","id":183596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=183019#post183019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make a variation of the Sacred Hunt aiming animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if proper Sacred Hunt is 2nd Dot Rite, I assume this one would be 1st Dot, yes? I don't want want them to pay too much for it, but you also have right it shouldn't be only &quot;you eat meat, you get 3 Essence&quot;. How much should Essence be generated from the Rite? Animals Stamina?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T01:24:52-07:00","id":183650,"title":"","content":"Making Essence easy to get from any animal tends to downplay the horror aspect of the temptation to eat human/wolf flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T02:35:58-07:00","id":183666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=183650#post183650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making Essence easy to get from any animal tends to downplay the horror aspect of the temptation to eat human/wolf flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taboo to restrictive to break is not broken in-game. It's like with Paradox in <b>Mage</b> - if it was Wisdom sin all the time, no player would choose it to mingle with Abyss. But if we made this personal players decision, he some time will slip Paradox outside, only to relive stressful situation and solve problem quickly. Then Scelasti shown to them is more &quot;it could be us if we don't restrain ourselves&quot;. More peronal horror added to game. Binding hands on taboos for players is making game <b>less</b> horrific. <br /> <br /> Then let's look on the thing with Essence generated by hunting animals. Players do this all the time as it's relative easy to do and - probably - not Harmony sin/Breaking Point for Spirit.<br /> <br /> Then comes dire need of large Essence. There are no animals in nearby, only humans. Players are more open on extreme solution, they previously done things lesser to other being. It is evil, but they done many times a thing a very like, a lesser evil of it. And they thinking.<br /> <br /> It makes interesting dilemma and also makes a bit use of our personal heads wiring that makes repetition standard answer in problem situations. And yes, it's a bit manipulation on players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T03:01:13-07:00","id":183670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=183666#post183666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Taboo to restrictive to break is not broken in-game. It's like with Paradox in <b>Mage</b> - if it was Wisdom sin all the time, no player would choose it to mingle with Abyss. But if we made this personal players decision, he some time will slip Paradox outside, only to relive stressful situation and solve problem quickly. Then Scelasti shown to them is more &quot;it could be us if we don't restrain ourselves&quot;. More peronal horror added to game. Binding hands on taboos for players is making game <b>less</b> horrific.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue here is that making hunting animals an easy and accessible source of Essence means the choice to hunt them or humans isn't much of a choice at all. If one can provide all the Essence a werewolf could want, and is lacking in moral quandaries, why bother with the other option? Hunting animals isn't really, you know, <i>horrific</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=183666#post183666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then comes dire need of large Essence. There are no animals in nearby, only humans. Players are more open on extreme solution, they previously done things lesser to other being. It is evil, but they done many times a thing a very like, a lesser evil of it. And they thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like too much of a niche situation. I mean, yeah I've seen it happen, but human flesh should probably be a temptation that rears it's head on a regular basis, as opposed to just life-or-limb situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":276,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","user":"Merkonan","date":". 06-29-2014, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T03:26:03-07:00","id":183676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=183670#post183670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue here is that making hunting animals an easy and accessible source of Essence means the choice to hunt them or humans isn't much of a choice at all. If one can provide all the Essence a werewolf could want, and is lacking in moral quandaries, why bother with the other option? Hunting animals isn't really, you know, <i>horrific</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand this, but my players need a way to collect large amounts of Essence to reinvigorate the Barren that is on the domain of they Totem spirit. As we play in &quot;non-human&quot; Territory ( closest human settlment is controlled by Bale Hounds ) they don't have any reasonable way to collect Essence. But animal hunting is not without they own problems - as our pack Alpha pointed out, they can't &quot;out hunt&quot; all animals in region, as both spirits and humans will notice. If region thriving with deers and foxes become too quite, it rie questions. And from question can quickly rose a hunters group...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=183670#post183670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like too much of a niche situation. I mean, yeah I've seen it happen, but human flesh should probably be a temptation that rears it's head on a regular basis, as opposed to just life-or-limb situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this, but it also would lead to &quot;our werewolves only think on flesh of humans&quot;. Best solution would be something like Kindred blood addiction, or maybe one level lower - characters maybe don't need the Essence all the time to survive and throw themselves on people, but they get HUNGRY when they low on it, looking on flesh as means to fill they gaps, possibly?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T06:56:26-07:00","id":183762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=182780#post182780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the other animals were generating small parts of Essence, how much it would be? I think probably one Essence point for whole deer, or maybe up to Stamina of animal. This way humans and wolves are still far superior prey (and even easier to hunt), but we have image of werewolves eating other animals on day-to-day scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Hunters in Darkness have a Milestone Gift that allows you to gain Essence from Animals. The gift allows one to regain Essence equal to 1 Point of Essence for each Health Box the Animal possessed. This assumes that you strip the carcass down to the bones.<br /> <br /> Also, normally, You gain Essence from Human Flesh equal to their Health Boxes Consumed.<br /> <br /> As for Collecting Essence - There is a Rite for that Already (Rite of the Sacred Hunt). Use that. It is a spiritual issue, so use the Essence harvested from the Spirits that you hunt to fix the Issue. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-29-2014, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T00:48:40-07:00","id":187767,"title":"","content":"Essence from eating humans is one point of Essence per point of lethal damage, making an average human worth 14 points of Essence.<br /> <br /> As for the pack's essence problem, if they are located in a remote area that doesn't have much human contact then they should be able to find some low level loci relatively easily, maybe even a higher level locus as well. Getting Essence just from hunting animals is a pretty fundamental change and it isn't one I'd recommend (or allow in a game I was running, unless you had the HiD Milestone Gift.) You as the ST control the amount of loci available, as well as their level, so you should be able to tailor the amount of Essence available to the players so that it meets your story's needs. You already have the necessary tools to do what you want without needing to change anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T12:24:58-07:00","id":188178,"title":"","content":"Well, there is a significant camp of gamers that like to create a world and allow the players to explore it, merely narrating how the world reacts to their actions. Not interfering and most definitely not changing anything about the world once it's created. I find them most often in the Pathfinder and OSR communities, but I'm sure there are some WoD fans who play this way, and their play style should be acknowledged. For those who do like to play this way, the loci are where they are and if the players don't find any of them, that's life. In which case, another means of acquiring essence anywhere could be worth considering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T14:07:16-07:00","id":188227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=188178#post188178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who do like to play this way, the loci are where they are and if the players don't find any of them, that's life. In which case, another means of acquiring essence anywhere could be worth considering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm probably one of them, as I'm old D&amp;D player also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But to highlight my problem - I don't like make things like &quot;oww, players don't have Essence source in the middle of nowhere, I must put them illogical sacred place that no one will attend&quot;. No, in my games they should create one themselves. But to not rewrite whole Essence usage chapter, they would need a BIG pool of Essence to begin process of creating Locus, especially, as their given one was on Barren. From where PCs will get like 150 points of Essence in times of couple session?<br /> <br /> And here comes hunting for flesh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T04:13:41-07:00","id":188637,"title":"","content":"And why wouldn't the werewolves just hunt spirits for essence? Spirits are pretty much omnipresent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T07:33:57-07:00","id":188688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=183596#post183596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if proper Sacred Hunt is 2nd Dot Rite, I assume this one would be 1st Dot, yes? I don't want want them to pay too much for it, but you also have right it shouldn't be only &quot;you eat meat, you get 3 Essence&quot;. How much should Essence be generated from the Rite? Animals Stamina?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got it the wrong way around; getting Essence from animals would be extremely powerful as an ability. It isn't a 'lesser' ability than a usual Sacred Hunt, it's a new tool that gives you access to Essence where normally you would not have it at all.<br /> <br /> As such, <i>if</i> one were to add a ritual that allows Essence to be taken from animals (I wouldn't personally add it), it should probably be a 5-dot rite of some sort and bear a very hefty drawback. I'd probably say something like it locks you into Urhan form for a month. Should probably have a non-Essence price attached too.<br /> <br /> There <i>is</i> a new one-dot Rite in IC that's a good source of Essence but it is <i>extremely</i> limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T08:13:32-07:00","id":188701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=188637#post188637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And why wouldn't the werewolves just hunt spirits for essence? Spirits are pretty much omnipresent.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a good point. Sacred Hunt already exists and there are spirits everywhere, so why make up a new version for hunting animals to give your players a source of Essence when spirits are probably more abundant than animals anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:02:48-07:00","id":188762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=188701#post188701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is a good point. Sacred Hunt already exists and there are spirits everywhere, so why make up a new version for hunting animals to give your players a source of Essence when spirits are probably more abundant than animals anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sacred Hunt on any spirit? It's a bit... hmmm, prosaic? I was thinking Uratha isn't choosing spirit to hunt because it's to close to home of them being half-spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:16:06-07:00","id":188770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=188762#post188762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sacred Hunt on any spirit? It's a bit... hmmm, prosaic? I was thinking Uratha isn't choosing spirit to hunt because it's to close to home of them being half-spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div> Spirits eat each other for essence all the time, that's just part of being a spirit. Wolves don't have any compunctions about eating other animals, why would werewolves have any about eating other spirits? <br /> <br /> And I didn't necessarily mean &quot;I call a hunt on all spirits!&quot;, I meant going after a specific spirit because you need it's essence. Think of the ritual as a Hunter offering respect and gratitude to his game for its sacrifice so that he may eat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T13:29:47-07:00","id":188903,"title":"","content":"If you need that much Essence, enough to heal a Barren, it shouldn't be a simple matter of collecting resources by eating animals. Needing that much essence, to me, would mean that the Pack will likely need to make a deal with a vastly potent spirit. A barren turned locus is already going to attract a huge amount of attention from spirits after theyre done, so why not offer a nice home to a godly spirit in exchange for funding the locus. In addition to the spirit, multiple packs of wolves joining ritual and essence together. Make it into a story rather than &quot;farming&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T21:39:41-07:00","id":189167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=188903#post188903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to the spirit, multiple packs of wolves joining ritual and essence together. Make it into a story rather than &quot;farming&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>When players are only other pack than Bale Hounds in nearby settlement mutliple werewolves aren't possible. Hunting for very powerfull spirit is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T22:39:27-07:00","id":189207,"title":"","content":"I imagine consuming Spirits for Essence <i>might </i>be a Breaking Point towards the Spirit side of Harmony, because doing as the Spirits do probably makes you more Spirit like.<br /> <br /> Which should be a cool thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T23:38:33-07:00","id":189217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=189207#post189207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine consuming Spirits for Essence <i>might </i>be a Breaking Point towards the Spirit side of Harmony, because doing as the Spirits do probably makes you more Spirit like.<br /> <br /> Which should be a cool thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Rites preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Uratha bring down a spirit, they may divide its remaining Essence amongst themselves as they see fit; this can be used to destroy a spirit by draining all its Essence and discorporating it, but doing so is usually a Breaking Point towards Spirit and is seen as disrespectful if done without good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, breaking off the hunt early is a Breaking Point towards human, so I guess calling a hunt on all spirits in the area, om-noming a big one, and then calling it a day would actually balance out in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T03:15:08-07:00","id":189275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, breaking off the hunt early is a Breaking Point towards human, so I guess calling a hunt on all spirits in the area, om-noming a big one, and then calling it a day would actually balance out in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, asumming the slide up or down the scale happens only one dot at a time regardless of the particular Breaking point. What if that's not the case and you moved one step towards Spirit for eating the Essence but moved two steps towards Flesh for calling the hunt off prematurely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  grammar 07-06-2014, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T07:02:34-07:00","id":189354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=189275#post189275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yep, asumming the slide up or down the scale happens only one dot at a time regardless of the particular Breaking point. What if that's not the case and you moved one step towards Spirit for eating the Essence but moved two steps towards Flesh for calling the hunt off prematurely?</div> </div> </div> </div> It also banks on failing both breaking point rolls, so even if failing only slides you one dot in either direction, it would still be an unreliable strategy. I just found it amusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T12:18:14-07:00","id":189549,"title":"","content":"Ah, true, forgot that rolling was still involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T23:23:42-07:00","id":189966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=189217#post189217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, breaking off the hunt early is a Breaking Point towards human, so I guess calling a hunt on all spirits in the area, om-noming a big one, and then calling it a day would actually balance out in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>When would Breaking Point be resolved? Just after Sacred Hunt done, and proper hunting started?<br /> <br /> Also - are Breaking Points limitd to some Integrity/Harmony levels? Like this thing from Scared Hunt is problem to Uratha with Harmony 6+ and lower it's not a problem? Or any time the werewolves are calling Sacred Hunt it's Breaking Point toward the Spirit?<br /> <br /> So if typical Rank 2 spirit in area has those 15 Essence, and players need 150 Essence so it's about 10 Sacred Hunts. If characters are having starting Harmony 7, and every Sacred Hunt is Breaking Point - it will make a pack a Z'iir before they end the mission.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T12:07:17-07:00","id":190606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/182714-hunger-for-flesh?p=189966#post189966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When would Breaking Point be resolved? Just after Sacred Hunt done, and proper hunting started?</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe I should clarify that I'm talking about the Rite &quot;Sacred Hunt&quot; that was in the Rites preview a couple of weeks ago. You can read it yourself of you would like, and make your own interpretations. Plus that was a first draft, so it may change by the time the book is released. But currently, it says that taking any significant action not related to the Hunt ends the Rite, and doing so before you have caught your prey is a Breaking Point towards human. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also - are Breaking Points limitd to some Integrity/Harmony levels? Like this thing from Scared Hunt is problem to Uratha with Harmony 6+ and lower it's not a problem? Or any time the werewolves are calling Sacred Hunt it's Breaking Point toward the Spirit? </div> </div> </div> Your guess is as good as mine. We all have access to the same spoilers and nothing else. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if typical Rank 2 spirit in area has those 15 Essence, and players need 150 Essence so it's about 10 Sacred Hunts. If characters are having starting Harmony 7, and every Sacred Hunt is Breaking Point - it will make a pack a Z'iir before they end the mission. </div> </div> </div> Remember, just because you experience a Breaking Point does not automatically mean you lose/gain Harmony. You still get your roll, and only if you fail does it shift. If the PCs are at 7 Harmony, presumably they still have a pretty good dice pool to resist, plus bonuses from Touchstones, and if you do fail a Breaking Point roll here or there, you can go do something that will be a Breaking Point towards Human. [/QUOTE]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}